cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AutoTuneNet or AutoTuneNet-Bench in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "AutoTuneNet: Online Hyperparameter Adaptation"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Raina
    given-names: Mitish
version: 1.0.2
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/mitishraina/AutoTuneNet"
url: "https://github.com/mitishraina/AutoTuneNet"
abstract: >-
  AutoTuneNet treats hyperparameter tuning as an online control problem inside a
  single training run. A Bayesian optimizer (Optuna TPE, ask-tell) proposes
  hyperparameters at each tuning step; proposals are applied with bounded updates,
  scored on a smoothed validation signal, and checked by a stability monitor that
  rolls back to the last known-good configuration on sustained regression.
  The repository includes AutoTuneNet-Bench, a benchmark suite for Online
  Hyperparameter Adaptation (OHA) under controlled non-stationarity.
keywords:
  - hyperparameter optimization
  - online hyperparameter adaptation
  - bayesian optimization
  - training stability
  - pytorch
